CAT = "s7Business"; SEG = "BUS"
Q = [
("A registered rep wants to send the same prepared market letter to 40 retail customers by email. Under FINRA Rule 2210 this is:",
 "A retail communication", ["Correspondence", "An institutional communication", "A public appearance"],
 "Rule 2210 treats a written message sent to more than 25 retail investors within any 30-calendar-day period as a retail communication. Twenty-five or fewer would be correspondence."),
("Who must approve most retail communications before they are first used?",
 "A registered principal", ["The branch office manager's assistant", "FINRA's Advertising Regulation staff", "The firm's outside auditor"],
 "Rule 2210 requires an appropriately qualified registered principal to approve retail communications before use or filing, with limited exceptions. FINRA reviews filed pieces but does not approve them."),
("A rep cold-calls a prospect who lives in another time zone. Under telemarketing rules, the call must be made:",
 "Between 8 a.m. and 9 p.m. the prospect's time", ["Between 8 a.m. and 9 p.m. the rep's time", "Between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m. the prospect's time", "During market hours in New York"],
 "FINRA Rule 3230 bars outbound telemarketing calls before 8 a.m. or after 9 p.m. at the called person's location. The caller's own clock does not matter."),
("A prospect asks a rep not to call again. How long must the firm honor that request on its own do-not-call list?",
 "Five years", ["One year", "Ninety days", "Eighteen months"],
 "A firm-specific do-not-call request must be honored for five years from when it was made. Eighteen months is the established business relationship window after a transaction."),
("Which call is permitted even though the person is on the national do-not-call registry?",
 "To a customer who traded 6 months ago", ["To a prospect on a purchased list", "To a referral given by a friend", "To a former customer gone 3 years"],
 "An established business relationship exists for 18 months after the customer's last transaction, so the call is allowed. A purchased list or a stale relationship gives no exemption."),
("A rep plans to sell real estate on weekends for a separate company and be paid for it. Before starting, the rep must:",
 "Give the firm prior written notice", ["Get prior approval from FINRA", "Notify the state realty board", "Inform customers in writing"],
 "FINRA Rule 3270 requires prior written notice to the member firm before an outside business activity for compensation. The firm then decides whether to limit or prohibit it."),
("A rep wants to help a friend's startup sell its stock to investors, for a fee, outside the firm. Under Rule 3280 the rep needs:",
 "Written approval from the firm", ["Only verbal notice to a manager", "A Series 79 registration first", "Approval from the issuer's lawyer"],
 "A private securities transaction for compensation needs written notice and the firm's written approval, and the firm must then record and supervise it as its own business."),
("A firm's retail investor relationship summary (Form CRS) must be delivered to a new retail investor:",
 "By the first recommendation, account or order", ["Within 30 days after the account is opened", "Only if the customer asks for a copy", "Along with the first trade confirmation"],
 "Under Regulation Best Interest's companion rule, Form CRS goes to a retail investor before or at the earliest of a recommendation, opening an account or placing an order."),
("A rep posts a general comment about the firm's services on a public social media page. It is generally treated as:",
 "A retail communication", ["Correspondence", "Institutional communication", "A private message"],
 "Static content posted on a public social media site is available to any retail investor, so it is a retail communication. Unscripted posts in an interactive forum are treated like public appearances."),
("A rep is invited to speak about retirement investing at a local library seminar. Under Rule 2210 the talk is:",
 "A public appearance", ["Correspondence", "An institutional communication", "A research report"],
 "Unscripted talks at seminars, forums and interviews are public appearances. Any slides or handouts used at the seminar are retail communications and need principal approval."),
("Which statement is prohibited in a retail communication about a corporate bond?",
 "That the bond is completely risk free", ["That the bond pays semiannual interest", "That the bond is callable after five years", "That the bond is rated by an agency"],
 "Rule 2210 prohibits false, exaggerated or promissory claims. Calling any corporate bond risk free is misleading; the other statements are factual features."),
("Under Regulation S-P, a broker-dealer must give retail customers a privacy notice:",
 "When the relationship begins", ["Only when the customer asks in writing", "Each time a trade settles", "Only when data is shared"],
 "Regulation S-P requires an initial privacy notice at the start of the customer relationship, explaining how nonpublic personal information is used and shared, and an opt-out where sharing with nonaffiliated third parties is planned."),
("A rep wants to borrow money from a customer who is not a family member or a lending institution. Under FINRA Rule 3240 this is:",
 "Allowed only if the firm's procedures permit it", ["Always allowed with a signed promissory note", "Allowed if the loan is under one year", "Allowed if the customer is over 65"],
 "Rule 3240 bars borrowing from or lending to customers unless the firm has written procedures allowing it and the arrangement fits one of the permitted categories, with notice to and approval from the firm where required."),
("A rep's personal website includes a customer's statement praising the rep's stock picks. Under FINRA rules, a testimonial in a retail communication:",
 "Must say it may not be typical", ["Is banned in every retail piece", "Needs prior approval from the SEC", "Must name the stocks the customer bought"],
 "Rule 2210(d)(6) permits testimonials in retail communications if they prominently disclose that the experience may not be representative of other customers' and is no guarantee of future success, and, if more than $100 was paid for it, that it is a paid testimonial."),
("A prospect at a seminar gives a rep a business card and asks for information. A follow-up call within three months is:",
 "Permitted as an inquiry relationship", ["Barred until the prospect places a trade", "Permitted only by mail or email", "Barred if the number is on the national list"],
 "An inquiry or application creates an established business relationship for three months, so a call is allowed even if the number is on the national registry."),
("A rep tells a prospect that a new fund's shares will be listed and \"guaranteed to rise in the first month.\" This is:",
 "A prohibited promissory claim", ["Acceptable if the rep believes it", "Acceptable in oral sales talk", "Acceptable with a risk disclosure"],
 "Predictions or projections of investment performance and promises of gains are prohibited in communications, whether written or oral. A disclaimer does not cure a misleading claim."),
]
